# Swift Package Manager
.build/
# Separate scratch path for the Linux container check (AGENTS.md), kept
# apart from .build so container runs and host macOS builds do not
# invalidate each other's caches.
.build-linux/
.swiftpm/
Packages/
Package.pins
# The root Package.resolved is committed: it pins the package's single
# remote dependency (ZIPFoundation, exact) and is a reviewable artifact.
# The PackageConsumerSmoke harness consumes only the RunPlayCore
# product, yet on macOS SwiftPM still resolves ZIPFoundation through
# the root path dependency and writes a lockfile here — pinned but
# never compiled. SwiftPM prunes unused package dependencies
# per-product at build planning but per-package at resolution, so a
# consumer pins transitive remotes it never links; on Linux the same
# graph is pruned earlier and no lockfile is written. This rule is
# load-bearing on macOS: do not remove it because Linux-only testing
# never sees the file. A committed lockfile for a disposable
# verification package would be sync burden with no benefit.
Tests/PackageConsumerSmoke/Package.resolved
*.xcodeproj

